(100, 'A2', 'Process Capability Assessment and Enhancement', 'Realize the process potential, stabilising and continuously improving process performance\r\n', '12', 8, '', '', 'Process control is based on feedback from customers or QC and basic awareness on statistical process tools.\r\nNo statistical processes are implemented to measure process performance.\r\nProcess capability is not monitored.\r\nNo concept of corrective actions.\r\n', 'Process control is done using control charts for monitoring performances in some cases.\r\nProcess performance measured and documented in an inspection sheet.\r\nShop floor is aware and measure process capability (Cp, Cpk) on adhoc basis.\r\nAdhoc corrective actions implemented.\r\n', 'Corrections are made to the processes on the basis of process trend.\r\nStatistical process implemented on 20-50% critical machines for process capability assessment.\r\n Process capability measured (Cp, Cpk) for 20%-50% critical processes and used for any improvement initiatives.\r\nAll corrective actions are implemented.\r\n', 'Process controlled using results from online SPC in <80>50-75% critical machines for process capability assessment.\r\nProcess capability measured (Cp, Cpk) for >50% and <75>=1.\r\nAll corrective actions are implemented and risk mitigation done to avoid similar issues elsewhere e.g. other lines.\r\n', 'Process controlled using results from online SPC in >80% critical machines.\r\nStatistical process implemented on >75% critical machines for process capability assessment.\r\nProcess capability measured (Cp, Cpk) for 75% critical processes, target value of Cpk>=1.33.\r\nAll corrective actions are implemented and risk mitigation done along with measurement of effectiveness.\r\n', 1, '2017-05-30 10:11:45', 1, '2017-05-30 16:41:45', 0),
(101, 'A5', 'Fire Safety', 'Planning and implementation of safe working against fire in the organisation\r\n', '13', 8, '', '', 'No focus on fire safety\r\nFire safety equipment are not adequate w.r.t the size of the plant and the no. of machines/ nature of production. Fire safety procedures are not practiced in the factory\r\nNo system for testing of fire safety equipment', 'Adhoc action taken on fire safety mostly when something goes wrong; Drill fire fighters and workers at least once every year\r\nBasic fire safety procedures and inadequate no. of fire safety equipment are available in few areas of factory only. Safety related records are not available\r\nSystem for testing of fire safety equipment are available but not followed\r\n', 'Fire fighting teams with limited fire fighter are placed at each section of the factory; Drill fire fighters and workers at least once every year; Fire fighters received regular training; Drill fire fighters and workers at least once every six months.\r\nStandard fire safety procedures are practiced in factory and are adequate including fire safety equipment. Safety related records are maintained. Install fire alarms in the factory. Electrical circuits are enclosed, insulated, earthed, properly fused, and not overloaded.; Combustible material are kept away from hot surfaces and open flames. Employees are provided awareness training on fire safety.\r\nAll fire safety equipment are tested at least once in two years.\r\n', 'Pictures of fire fighters are prominently displayed for all workers to see.; Fire fighters are in proportional to the total workforce for each section of the factory with a clear identification badge; Fire fighters received regular training; Drill fire fighters and workers at least once every six months.\r\nSafety records are up to date and demonstrate very safe condition of operations.; Installed back-up lighting and water supplies in case the electricity or water mains are affected by fire.\r\nAll fire safety equipment are tested at least once per year and is in good condition\r\n', 'Pictures of fire fighters are prominently displayed for all workers to see.; Fire fighters must be part of a larger safety team that includes first aid coordinators, evaluation coordinators, etc.\r\nAn emergency plan which includes evacuation procedures in place; Run a factory inspection to determine where hazards are.\r\nAll fire safety equipment are tested at least two times per year and is in good condition.; All fire safety equipment are easy to get to in case of an emergency and that signage is clearly visible\r\n', 1, '2017-06-01 06:04:41', 1, '2017-06-01 11:34:41', 1),
(102, 'A2', 'Process Capability Assessment and Enhancement', 'Realize the process potential, stabilising and continuously improving process performance\r\n', '14', 8, '', '', 'Process control is based on feedback from customers or QC and basic awareness on statistical process tools.\r\nNo statistical processes are implemented to measure process performance.\r\nProcess capability is not monitored.\r\nNo concept of corrective actions.\r\n', 'Process control is done using control charts for monitoring performances in some cases.\r\nProcess performance measured and documented in an inspection sheet.\r\nShop floor is aware and measure process capability (Cp, Cpk) on adhoc basis.\r\nAdhoc corrective actions implemented.\r\n', 'Corrections are made to the processes on the basis of process trend.\r\nStatistical process implemented on 20-50% critical machines for process capability assessment.\r\n Process capability measured (Cp, Cpk) for 20%-50% critical processes and used for any improvement initiatives.\r\nAll corrective actions are implemented.\r\n', 'Process controlled using results from online SPC in <80>50-75% critical machines for process capability assessment.\r\nProcess capability measured (Cp, Cpk) for >50% and <75>=1.\r\nAll corrective actions are implemented and risk mitigation done to avoid similar issues elsewhere e.g. other lines.\r\n', 'Process controlled using results from online SPC in >80% critical machines.\r\nStatistical process implemented on >75% critical machines for process capability assessment.\r\nProcess capability measured (Cp, Cpk) for 75% critical processes, target value of Cpk>=1.33.\r\nAll corrective actions are implemented and risk mitigation done along with measurement of effectiveness.\r\n', 1, '2017-05-30 10:11:45', 1, '2017-05-30 16:41:45', 0),
