(167, 'A5', 'Safe Working Environment', 'Planning for implementation for safe working of all processes and personnel', '7', 8, '', '', 'No formal safety policy in place\r\nNo communication on safety policy\r\nNo training imparted on safety\r\nSafety related accidents are attended reactively\r\nNo reviews done for safety techniques\r\nNo specific system for investigation of accidents/incidents\r\n', 'Safety policy briefly mentioned in overall company policy\r\nCommunication imparted on safety policy to employees, but not followed by a regular schedule\r\nTraining imparted but no regular schedule\r\nMajor safety incidents are investigated and CAPAs taken\r\nReviews for safety techniques done on adhoc basis\r\nMinimal process to avoid fines and complaints on safety conditions\r\n', 'Formal safety policy exists and addresses issues related to employees and contract workers\r\nSafety policy displayed in the factory, regular communication is followed.; Safety day/week/month is celebrated\r\nFormal/informal safety training done e.g. mock drill\r\n Safety techniques demonstrated through visual management, safety information reviewed in detail on periodic basis\r\nDaily safety dashboard established, frequent reviews planned and documented\r\nSOPs established to meet statutory and regulatory requirements on safety\r\n', ' Formal safety policy addresses the concern of suppliers and community at large in addition to employees and contract workers\r\nSafety policy communicated through comprehensive means (display in notice board, employees handbook)\r\n Classroom and practical sessions on safety done for 100% employees\r\n Safety information reviewed, leading to identification and implementation of CAPAs\r\n “Near Misses” with respect to safety are recorded, analysed and acted upon. CAPAs are documented and reviewed\r\n SOP established for safe working environment throughout the factory\r\n', ' Formal safety policy addresses the concern of all primary and secondary stakeholders, along with sustainability goals\r\n Safety policy reinforced everyday during meetings / speech e.g. start daily meeting with focus on safety\r\n Training effectiveness measured for all safety related training with safety audits in place showing 90?herence\r\n Step by step risk management plan in place. Poka-yoke for safety have been done as per industry benchmark\r\n Pro-active and preventive steps are in place for safety techniques and visual management is in place\r\n Organisation has OHSAS system in place. Well established system of Hazard Identification & Risk Assessment for all processes\r\n', 1, '2017-05-30 10:20:22', 1, '2017-05-30 16:50:22', 0),
(168, 'A5', 'Safe Working Environment', 'Planning for implementation for safe working of all processes and personnel', '8', 8, '', '', 'No formal safety policy in place\r\nNo communication on safety policy\r\nNo training imparted on safety\r\nSafety related accidents are attended reactively\r\nNo reviews done for safety techniques\r\nNo specific system for investigation of accidents/incidents\r\n', 'Safety policy briefly mentioned in overall company policy\r\nCommunication imparted on safety policy to employees, but not followed by a regular schedule\r\nTraining imparted but no regular schedule\r\nMajor safety incidents are investigated and CAPAs taken\r\nReviews for safety techniques done on adhoc basis\r\nMinimal process to avoid fines and complaints on safety conditions\r\n', 'Formal safety policy exists and addresses issues related to employees and contract workers\r\nSafety policy displayed in the factory, regular communication is followed.; Safety day/week/month is celebrated\r\nFormal/informal safety training done e.g. mock drill\r\n Safety techniques demonstrated through visual management, safety information reviewed in detail on periodic basis\r\nDaily safety dashboard established, frequent reviews planned and documented\r\nSOPs established to meet statutory and regulatory requirements on safety\r\n', ' Formal safety policy addresses the concern of suppliers and community at large in addition to employees and contract workers\r\nSafety policy communicated through comprehensive means (display in notice board, employees handbook)\r\n Classroom and practical sessions on safety done for 100% employees\r\n Safety information reviewed, leading to identification and implementation of CAPAs\r\n “Near Misses” with respect to safety are recorded, analysed and acted upon. CAPAs are documented and reviewed\r\n SOP established for safe working environment throughout the factory\r\n', ' Formal safety policy addresses the concern of all primary and secondary stakeholders, along with sustainability goals\r\n Safety policy reinforced everyday during meetings / speech e.g. start daily meeting with focus on safety\r\n Training effectiveness measured for all safety related training with safety audits in place showing 90?herence\r\n Step by step risk management plan in place. Poka-yoke for safety have been done as per industry benchmark\r\n Pro-active and preventive steps are in place for safety techniques and visual management is in place\r\n Organisation has OHSAS system in place. Well established system of Hazard Identification & Risk Assessment for all processes\r\n', 1, '2017-05-30 10:20:22', 1, '2017-05-30 16:50:22', 0),
