(334, 'C4', 'Process Control', 'Application of statistical quality control method,   to monitor and control processes, to identify variances as a basis for continual improvement\r\n', '30', 10, '', '', 'No standards/SOPs available to define control plans\r\nNo documented process control plan improvement in place\r\nNo approach exists for process control\r\nNo concept of CAPA to address variances in processes\r\n', 'SOPs / work instructions initiated to control few critical/key processes\r\nProcess control plans in place with adherence &lt;40%\r\nProcess control approach followed on adhoc basis\r\nCAPA to control variances identified in &lt;50% critical processes\r\n', 'Details SOPs / Work instructions are available basis control plans to ease the process understanding\r\nProcess control plans in place with adherence 40%-60%\r\n Process control approach available for critical processes\r\nCAPAs to control variances identified in >50% critical processes\r\n', ' Frequent revisions are made in Control plans / SOPs and work instructions basis any process change. Product samples (First piece inspection) are also kept near workstation for referencing purpose\r\nProcess control plans in place with adherence >60%-90%\r\n Process control approach available and scope well defined for all processes\r\nCAPAs to control variances are identified and implemented in all cases\r\n', ' Electronic version of control plans / SOPs / Work instructions are deployed\r\nProcess control plans in place with adherence >90%\r\n Online controls in place for process controls\r\nCAPAs to control variances taken in all cases and recorded, effectiveness is also measured\r\n', 1, '2017-05-30 10:43:26', 1, '2017-05-30 17:13:26', 0),
(335, 'D1', 'Design Capability', 'Have internal resources or access to design capabilities to enable the designing (including design of experiment, design failure mode and effect analysis, selection and inspection of key characteristics), development and constant up gradation of product and service features. Ensure that product meets the specification requirements for all identified operational conditions (such as High temperature test, Low temperature test, Vibration test, Dust test, Driving rain test, Shock or Impact test etc)\r\n', '7', 11, '', '', 'Organization has no design function, changes are made as and when required\r\nNo process exists for making design improvements\r\nNo monitoring/assessment of design capability\r\n', 'Organization has design and development groups to design product as per customer needs\r\nDesign improvements are based on inhouse knowledge with some customer inputs\r\nDesign capability is assessed on a reactive basis e.g. an index of customer complaints and extent of failures found during manufacturing\r\n', ' Design group in place with design review a common practice\r\n Life Testing - Normal and accelerated performed on samples for design improvements but results not evaluated\r\nDesign capability is proactively assessed e.g. based on variation in product performance and analysis between actual and target performance\r\n', ' Design group in place with proactive design capability. All possible reasons for low capability are investigated\r\n Design for Reliability (DFR) in place incorporating risk analysis and DFMEA conducted\r\nDesign capability is continuously assessed. Benchmarks are used to compare capability on various design characteristics. There is at least 1 design patent / IPR filed\r\n', ' Proactive design planning by design group  + Active market research for meeting future needs and Capability is improved by analysing low capability areas\r\n Creative solutions are determined basis the tools like Prioritization matrix . Redesign performed basis DFR , customer feedback and internal failures\r\nProduct design capability is assessed in sigma level through a comprehensive score card incorporating several elements including parts, processes and performance. There are at least 2 design patent / IPR available.\r\n', 2, '2017-05-31 03:16:17', 1, '2017-05-31 00:03:00', 0),
(336, 'D1', 'Design Capability', 'Have internal resources or access to design capabilities to enable the designing (including design of experiment, design failure mode and effect analysis, selection and inspection of key characteristics), development and constant up gradation of product and service features. Ensure that product meets the specification requirements for all identified operational conditions (such as High temperature test, Low temperature test, Vibration test, Dust test, Driving rain test, Shock or Impact test etc)\r\n', '8', 11, '', '', 'Organization has no design function, changes are made as and when required\r\nNo process exists for making design improvements\r\nNo monitoring/assessment of design capability\r\n', 'Organization has design and development groups to design product as per customer needs\r\nDesign improvements are based on inhouse knowledge with some customer inputs\r\nDesign capability is assessed on a reactive basis e.g. an index of customer complaints and extent of failures found during manufacturing\r\n', ' Design group in place with design review a common practice\r\n Life Testing - Normal and accelerated performed on samples for design improvements but results not evaluated\r\nDesign capability is proactively assessed e.g. based on variation in product performance and analysis between actual and target performance\r\n', ' Design group in place with proactive design capability. All possible reasons for low capability are investigated\r\n Design for Reliability (DFR) in place incorporating risk analysis and DFMEA conducted\r\nDesign capability is continuously assessed. Benchmarks are used to compare capability on various design characteristics. There is at least 1 design patent / IPR filed\r\n', ' Proactive design planning by design group  + Active market research for meeting future needs and Capability is improved by analysing low capability areas\r\n Creative solutions are determined basis the tools like Prioritization matrix . Redesign performed basis DFR , customer feedback and internal failures\r\nProduct design capability is assessed in sigma level through a comprehensive score card incorporating several elements including parts, processes and performance. There are at least 2 design patent / IPR available.\r\n', 2, '2017-05-31 03:16:17', 1, '2017-05-31 00:03:00', 0),
(337, 'D1', 'Design Capability', 'Have internal resources or access to design capabilities to enable the designing (including design of experiment, design failure mode and effect analysis, selection and inspection of key characteristics), development and constant up gradation of product and service features. Ensure that product meets the specification requirements for all identified operational conditions (such as High temperature test, Low temperature test, Vibration test, Dust test, Driving rain test, Shock or Impact test etc)\r\n', '9', 11, '', '', 'Organization has no design function, changes are made as and when required\r\nNo process exists for making design improvements\r\nNo monitoring/assessment of design capability\r\n', 'Organization has design and development groups to design product as per customer needs\r\nDesign improvements are based on inhouse knowledge with some customer inputs\r\nDesign capability is assessed on a reactive basis e.g. an index of customer complaints and extent of failures found during manufacturing\r\n', ' Design group in place with design review a common practice\r\n Life Testing - Normal and accelerated performed on samples for design improvements but results not evaluated\r\nDesign capability is proactively assessed e.g. based on variation in product performance and analysis between actual and target performance\r\n', ' Design group in place with proactive design capability. All possible reasons for low capability are investigated\r\n Design for Reliability (DFR) in place incorporating risk analysis and DFMEA conducted\r\nDesign capability is continuously assessed. Benchmarks are used to compare capability on various design characteristics. There is at least 1 design patent / IPR filed\r\n', ' Proactive design planning by design group  + Active market research for meeting future needs and Capability is improved by analysing low capability areas\r\n Creative solutions are determined basis the tools like Prioritization matrix . Redesign performed basis DFR , customer feedback and internal failures\r\nProduct design capability is assessed in sigma level through a comprehensive score card incorporating several elements including parts, processes and performance. There are at least 2 design patent / IPR available.\r\n', 2, '2017-05-31 03:16:17', 1, '2017-05-31 00:03:00', 0),
(338, 'D1', 'Design Capability', 'Have internal resources or access to design capabilities to enable the designing, development and constant up gradation of product and service features', '10', 11, '', '', 'No monitoring/assessment of design capability\r\nOrganization has no design function, changes are made as and when required\r\nNo process exists for making design improvements.; Uses traditional methods like point papers for weaving, etc.\r\n', 'Monitoring/assessment of design capability is in place but not followed\r\nOrganization has design and development groups to design product as per customer needs\r\nDesign capability is improved by design modification as necessitated by customer complaints or internal failures.; Developing design capability and building understanding of properties of yarn, fabric and dyes, techniques of sizing, etc.\r\n', 'Design capability is assessed on a reactive basis e.g an index of customer complaints and extent of failures found during manufacturing\r\nDesign group in place with design review being a common practice\r\n Life Testing -Normal and accelerated performed on samples for design improvements but results not evaluated.; IT enabled design tools and implementation of design processes like QFD\r\n', 'Design capability is proactively assessed e.g.. based on variation in product performance and analysis between actual and target performance. Capability levels are monitored to maintain high levels\r\nDesign group in place with proactive Design capability. All possible reasons for low capability are investigated\r\n All possible reasons for low capability are investigated using several tools/techniques- e.g.. seven tools, FMEA and DOE\r\n', 'Product design capability is assessed in sigma level through a comprehensive score card incorporating several elements including parts, processes and performance.\r\nProactive design planning by design group \r\nCapability is improved by analysing and improving characteristics on each aspect in low capability areas.\r\n', 2, '2017-06-01 03:10:01', 1, '2017-05-31 10:46:44', 1),
(339, 'D1', 'Design Capability', 'Have internal resources or access to design capabilities to enable the designing (including design of experiment, design failure mode and effect analysis, selection and inspection of key characteristics), development and constant up gradation of product and service features. Ensure that product meets the specification requirements for all identified operational conditions (such as High temperature test, Low temperature test, Vibration test, Dust test, Driving rain test, Shock or Impact test etc)\r\n', '11', 11, '', '', 'Organization has no design function, changes are made as and when required\r\nNo process exists for making design improvements\r\nNo monitoring/assessment of design capability\r\n', 'Organization has design and development groups to design product as per customer needs\r\nDesign improvements are based on inhouse knowledge with some customer inputs\r\nDesign capability is assessed on a reactive basis e.g. an index of customer complaints and extent of failures found during manufacturing\r\n', ' Design group in place with design review a common practice\r\n Life Testing - Normal and accelerated performed on samples for design improvements but results not evaluated\r\nDesign capability is proactively assessed e.g. based on variation in product performance and analysis between actual and target performance\r\n', ' Design group in place with proactive design capability. All possible reasons for low capability are investigated\r\n Design for Reliability (DFR) in place incorporating risk analysis and DFMEA conducted\r\nDesign capability is continuously assessed. Benchmarks are used to compare capability on various design characteristics. There is at least 1 design patent / IPR filed\r\n', ' Proactive design planning by design group  + Active market research for meeting future needs and Capability is improved by analysing low capability areas\r\n Creative solutions are determined basis the tools like Prioritization matrix . Redesign performed basis DFR , customer feedback and internal failures\r\nProduct design capability is assessed in sigma level through a comprehensive score card incorporating several elements including parts, processes and performance. There are at least 2 design patent / IPR available.\r\n', 2, '2017-06-01 03:10:01', 1, '2017-05-31 00:03:00', 0),
(340, 'D1', 'Design Capability', 'Have internal resources or access to design capabilities to enable the designing, development and constant up gradation of product and service features', '12', 11, '', '', 'No monitoring/assessment of design capability\r\nOrganization has no design function, changes are made as and when required\r\nNo process exists for making design improvements.; Uses traditional methods like point papers for weaving, etc.\r\n', 'Monitoring/assessment of design capability is in place but not followed\r\nOrganization has design and development groups to design product as per customer needs\r\nDesign capability is improved by design modification as necessitated by customer complaints or internal failures.; Developing design capability and building understanding of properties of yarn, fabric and dyes, techniques of sizing, etc.\r\n', 'Design capability is assessed on a reactive basis e.g an index of customer complaints and extent of failures found during manufacturing\r\nDesign group in place with design review being a common practice\r\n Life Testing -Normal and accelerated performed on samples for design improvements but results not evaluated.; IT enabled design tools and implementation of design processes like QFD\r\n', 'Design capability is proactively assessed e.g.. based on variation in product performance and analysis between actual and target performance. Capability levels are monitored to maintain high levels\r\nDesign group in place with proactive Design capability. All possible reasons for low capability are investigated\r\n All possible reasons for low capability are investigated using several tools/techniques- e.g.. seven tools, FMEA and DOE\r\n', 'Product design capability is assessed in sigma level through a comprehensive score card incorporating several elements including parts, processes and performance.\r\nProactive design planning by design group \r\n Capability is improved by analysing and improving characteristics on each aspect in low capability areas.\r\n', 2, '2017-06-01 03:10:01', 1, '2017-05-31 10:46:37', 1),
(341, 'D1', 'Design Capability', 'Have internal resources or access to design capabilities to enable the designing (including design of experiment, design failure mode and effect analysis, selection and inspection of key characteristics), development and constant up gradation of product and service features. Ensure that product meets the specification requirements for all identified operational conditions (such as High temperature test, Low temperature test, Vibration test, Dust test, Driving rain test, Shock or Impact test etc)\r\n', '13', 11, '', '', 'Organization has no design function, changes are made as and when required\r\nNo process exists for making design improvements\r\nNo monitoring/assessment of design capability\r\n', 'Organization has design and development groups to design product as per customer needs\r\nDesign improvements are based on inhouse knowledge with some customer inputs\r\nDesign capability is assessed on a reactive basis e.g. an index of customer complaints and extent of failures found during manufacturing\r\n', ' Design group in place with design review a common practice\r\n Life Testing - Normal and accelerated performed on samples for design improvements but results not evaluated\r\nDesign capability is proactively assessed e.g. based on variation in product performance and analysis between actual and target performance\r\n', ' Design group in place with proactive design capability. All possible reasons for low capability are investigated\r\n Design for Reliability (DFR) in place incorporating risk analysis and DFMEA conducted\r\nDesign capability is continuously assessed. Benchmarks are used to compare capability on various design characteristics. There is at least 1 design patent / IPR filed\r\n', ' Proactive design planning by design group  + Active market research for meeting future needs and Capability is improved by analysing low capability areas\r\n Creative solutions are determined basis the tools like Prioritization matrix . Redesign performed basis DFR , customer feedback and internal failures\r\nProduct design capability is assessed in sigma level through a comprehensive score card incorporating several elements including parts, processes and performance. There are at least 2 design patent / IPR available.\r\n', 2, '2017-06-01 03:10:01', 1, '2017-05-31 00:03:00', 0),
