(363, 'D2', 'Packaging Capability', 'Packing materials and methods of packing used for effective handling', '11', 11, '', '', 'Manual Packing and no control on Packing Material\r\nNo concept of corrective actions to improve processes to ensure packaging requirements\r\n', 'Manual Packing with proper control on Packing Material\r\nAdhoc corrective actions implemented to improve processes to ensure packaging requirements\r\n', 'Manual filling and semi-automated sealing with control on packing material; Packing material supplier provides certificate of analysis ensuring food-comfortable material\r\nAll corrective actions are implemented to improve processes to ensure packaging requirements\r\n', 'Semi automated filling and fully automated sealing methods with control on packing material; Packing material supplier provides certificate of analysis per consignment to ensure food-comfortable packing material\r\nAll corrective actions are implemented and risk mitigation done to avoid similar issues elsewhere e.g. other products\r\n', 'Fully automated packing system with packing material control; Packing material supplier provides certificate of analysis per consignment to ensure food-comfortable packing material\r\nAll corrective actions are implemented and risk mitigation done along with measurement of effectiveness\r\n', 1, '2017-06-01 04:55:37', 1, '2017-06-01 10:25:37', 1),
(364, 'D2', 'Design Process and Methodologies', 'Have a systematic approach for design, review and validation to ensure product design meets customer needs and expectations\r\n', '12', 11, '', '', 'No process of design planning\r\nNo design validation studies done\r\nAll the designs are reviewed by customers only, Change control process is not followed\r\n', 'Design planning ensures customer requirements are met\r\nDesign Validation studies done but no prototyping done\r\nReactive approach in place for review and error rectification in designs\r\n', 'Design planning to ensure that the customer specifications and regulatory requirements are met\r\nDesign validation done at SME through prototyping\r\nCustomer complaints with respect to designs are maintained with reasons for failures investigated & suitable actions taken for prevention\r\n', 'Design planning to ensure that the customer specifications and regulatory requirements are met\r\nDesign validation done at SME through prototyping\r\nCustomer complaints with respect to designs are maintained with reasons for failures investigated & suitable actions taken for prevention\r\n', ' Simulation tools like FEA, CAD, CAE done to create design\r\nDesign validation done through simulation at SME R&D\r\n Designs are optimized for robustness using QE techniques as suggested in ISO 16336 on RPD (Robust Parameter Design) and Takes IPR for designs\r\n', 1, '2017-05-31 05:34:41', 1, '2017-05-31 00:04:41', 0),
(365, 'D2', 'Batch release process', 'Describe the procedure for Release / Rejection of products which are intended for dispatch\r\n', '13', 11, '', '', 'No process of design planning\r\nNo design validation studies done\r\nAll the designs are reviewed by customers only, Change control process is not followed\r\n', 'Design planning ensures customer requirements are met\r\nDesign Validation studies done but no prototyping done\r\nReactive approach in place for review and error rectification in designs\r\n', 'Design planning to ensure that the customer specifications and regulatory requirements are met\r\nDesign validation done at SME through prototyping\r\nCustomer complaints with respect to designs are maintained with reasons for failures investigated & suitable actions taken for prevention\r\n', 'Design planning to ensure that the customer specifications and regulatory requirements are met\r\nDesign validation done at SME through prototyping\r\nCustomer complaints with respect to designs are maintained with reasons for failures investigated & suitable actions taken for prevention\r\n', ' Simulation tools like FEA, CAD, CAE done to create design\r\nDesign validation done through simulation at SME R&D\r\n Designs are optimized for robustness using QE techniques as suggested in ISO 16336 on RPD (Robust Parameter Design) and Takes IPR for designs\r\n', 1, '2017-06-01 07:06:16', 1, '2017-06-01 12:36:16', 1),
(366, 'D2', 'Batch Release Process', 'Describe the procedure for Release / Rejection of products which are intended for dispatch\r\n', '14', 11, '', '', 'No review mechanism exists\r\nNo targets set for batch release\r\nNo quality control unit in place to test quality of outgoing batches\r\n', 'Review done on need basis - mostly when the backlog increases\r\nTargets set and &lt;50% targets are met\r\nIndependent quality control unit in place with full authority to approve or reject all batches\r\n', 'Standard review mechanism is established; Reviews happen regularly\r\nTargets set and 50-75% targets are met\r\n Detailed SOPs/protocols governing batch release in place including detailed approach in the event of out of specification (OOS results) as well as measures to ensure rejected, under-analysis and approved batches are physically separated\r\n', ' Review mechanism with periodic reviews done by top management\r\nTargets set and >75-95% targets are met\r\n Batch release SOP/protocols take into consideration other elements beyond analytical test results of particular batch such as: Incidents or deviations during production of the batch. OOS results observed in other batches which may indicate risk for particular batch being considered for approval/rejection e.g. Batches which may have been tested in same sequence\r\n', ' Review cadence established and periodic review done by top management, dashboards published on regular basis and improvements tracked\r\nTargets set and >95% targets are met\r\n Management systems in place to continously monitor batch release, customer complaints, batch rejections and track repeat failures. Efforts to continuously improve these metrics undertaken through the investigation and CAPA process\r\n', 1, '2017-05-31 03:35:58', 1, '2017-05-31 09:05:58', 1),
(367, 'D2', 'Batch Release Process', 'Describe the procedure for Release / Rejection of products which are intended for dispatch\r\n', '15', 11, '', '', 'No targets set for batch release\r\nNo quality control unit in place to test quality of outgoing batches\r\n', 'Targets set and &lt;50% targets are met\r\nIndependent quality control unit in place with full authority to approve or reject all batches\r\n', 'Targets set and 50-75% targets are met\r\n Detailed SOPs/protocols governing batch release in place including detailed approach in the event of out of specification (OOS results) as well as measures to ensure rejected, under-analysis and approved batches are physically separated\r\n', 'Targets set and >75-95% targets are met\r\n Batch release SOP/protocols take into consideration other elements beyond analytical test results of particular batch such as: Incidents or deviations during production of the batch. OOS results observed in other batches which may indicate risk for particular batch being considered for approval/rejection e.g. Batches which may have been tested in same sequence\r\n', 'Targets set and >95% targets are met\r\n Management systems in place to continously monitor batch release, customer complaints, batch rejections and track repeat failures. Efforts to continuously improve these metrics undertaken through the investigation and CAPA process\r\n', 1, '2017-05-31 03:47:08', 1, '2017-05-31 09:17:08', 1),
