ormed basis DFR, customer feedback and internal failures.\r\nProduct design capability is assessed in sigma level through a comprehensive score card incorporating several elements including parts, processes and performance. There are at least 2 design patent / IPR available.', 1, '2017-06-01 09:14:40', 1, '2017-06-01 03:44:40', 0),
(1315, 'A6', 'Fire Safety', 'Planning and implementation of safe working against fire in the organisation\r\n', '11', 8, '', '', 'No focus on fire safety\r\nFire safety equipment are not adequate w.r.t the size of the plant and the no. of machines/ nature of production. Fire safety procedures are not practiced in the factory\r\nNo system for testing of fire safety equipment\r\n', 'Adhoc action taken on fire safety mostly when something goes wrong\r\nBasic fire safety procedures and inadequate no. of fire safety equipments are available in few areas of factory only. Safety related records are not available\r\nSystem for testing of fire safety equipment are available but not followed', 'Fire fighting teams with limited fire fighter are placed at each section of the factory; Drill fire fighters and workers at least once every year\r\nStandard fire safety procedures are practiced in factory and are adequate including fire safety equipments. Safety related records are maintained; Install fire alarms in the factory ; Electrical circuits are enclosed, insulated, earthed, properly fused, and not overloaded.; Combustible material are kept away from hot surfaces and open flames.; Employees are provided awareness training on fire safety.\r\nAll fire safety equipment are tested at least once in two years.', 'Fire fighters are in proportion to the total workforce for each section of the factory with a clear identification badge; Fire fighters received regular training; Drill fire fighters and workers at least once every six months.\r\nSafety records are up to date and demonstrate very safe condition of operations.; Installed back-up lighting and water supplies in case the electricity or water mains are affected by fire.\r\nAll fire safety equipment are tested at least once per year and is in good condition', 'Pictures of fire fighters are prominently displayed for all workers to see.; Fire fighters must be part of a larger safety team that includes first aid coordinators, evaluation coordinators, etc.\r\nAn emergency plan which includes evacuation procedures in place.; Runs a factory inspection to determine where hazards are.\r\nAll fire safety equipment are tested at least two times per year and is in good condition.; All fire safety equipment are easy to get to in case of an emergency and that signage is clearly visible\r\n', 1, '2017-06-01 10:06:02', 1, '2017-06-01 04:36:02', 0),
(1316, 'C5', 'Analytical Process Validation', 'Process used to confirm that the analytical procedure employed for specific test is suitable for its intended use\r\n', '18', 10, '', '', 'No concept of method validation, methods provided by customers\r\nNo validation of analytical methods in place or methods provided by customer\r\nNo concept of corrective actions to improve methods\r\n', 'Analytical method validation is planned for only critical FG, no dedicated analytical method validation team in place\r\nAnalytical methods validated for critical finished goods\r\nAdhoc corrective actions implemented to improve methods\r\n', 'Analytical method validation is planned for FG, RM and Intermediates, no dedicated analytical method validation team in place\r\nAnalytical methods for RM, FG, Intermediate and in-process validated. Plan in place to complete validation for remaining methods\r\nAll corrective actions are implemented to improve methods and documented\r\n', 'Separate analytical method validation team in place for transferring methods to plant QC lab post validation\r\nAll analytical methods for commercialized products validated. QC inputs built into analytical method development through informal processes (QC feedback into analytical method development)\r\nAll corrective actions are implemented and risk mitigation done to avoid similar issues elsewhere e.g. other products or methods\r\n', 'Dedicated team in place for taking over analytical method transfers in QC from the central method validation team\r\nQC inputs built into analytical method development through a formal process to ensure productivity and quality. Structured process to transfer methods from R&D to factory\r\nAll corrective actions are implemented and risk mitigation done along with measurement of effectiveness of method improvement measures\r\n', 1, '2017-06-01 05:39:42', 1, '2017-06-01 11:09:42', 1),
(1317, 'D3', 'Data Integrity', 'Maintenance of and assurance of accuracy and consistency of data over its entire life-cycle\r\n', '18', 11, '', '', 'No quality control unit in place to test quality of outgoing batches\r\nNo targets set for batch release\r\nNo review mechanism exists\r\n', 'Independent quality control unit in place with full authority to approve or reject all batches\r\nTargets set and &lt;50% targets are met\r\nReview done on need basis - mostly when the backlog increases\r\n', 'Detailed SOPs/protocols governing batch release in place including detailed approach in the event of out of specification (OOS results) as well as measures to ensure rejected, under-analysis and approved batches are physically separated\r\nTargets set and 50-75% targets are met\r\nStandard review mechanism is established; Reviews happen regularly\r\n', 'Batch release SOP/protocols take into consideration other elements beyond analytical test results of particular batch such as: Incidents or deviations during production of the batch. OOS results observed in other batches which may indicate risk for particular batch being considered for approval/rejection e.g. Batches which may have been tested in same sequence\r\nTargets set and 75-95% targets are met\r\nReview mechanism with periodic reviews done by top management\r\n', 'Management systems in place to continuously monitor batch release, customer complaints, batch rejections and track repeat failures. Efforts to continuously improve these metrics undertaken through the investigation and CAPA process\r\nTargets set and >95% targets are met\r\nReview cadence established and periodic review done by top management, dashboards published on regular basis and improvements tracked\r\n', 1, '2017-06-01 05:43:51', 1, '2017-06-01 11:13:51', 1),
(1318, 'D3', 'Batch Release Process', 'Describe the procedure for Release / Rejection of products which are intended for dispatch\r\n', '7', 11, '', '', 'No quality control unit in place to test quality of outgoing batches\r\nNo targets set for batch release\r\nNo review mechanism exists\r\n', 'Independent quality control unit in place with full authority to approve or reject all batches\r\nTargets set and &lt;50% targets are met\r\nReview done on need basis - mostly when the backlog increases\r\n', 'Detailed SOPs/protocols governing batch release in place including detailed approach in the event of out of specification (OOS results) as well as measures to ensure rejected, under-analysis and approved batches are physically separated\r\nTargets set and 50-75% targets are met\r\nStandard review mechanism is established; Reviews happen regularly\r\n', 'Batch release SOP/protocols take into consideration other elements beyond analytical test results of particular batch such as: Incidents or deviations during production of the batch. OOS results observed in other batches which may indicate risk for particular batch being considered for approval/rejection e.g. Batches which may have been tested in same sequence\r\nTargets set and >75-95% targets are met\r\nReview mechanism with periodic reviews done by top management', 'Management systems in place to continuously monitor batch release, customer complaints, batch rejections and track repeat failures. Efforts to continuously improve these metrics undertaken through the investigation and CAPA process\r\nTargets set and &lt;95% targets are met\r\nReview cadence established and periodic review done by top management, dashboards published on regular basis and improvements tracked', 1, '2017-06-01 05:57:48', 1, '2017-06-01 11:27:48', 1),
